        "dimensions": [
          "syntax",
          "concept"
        ],
        "text": "should提出建议；allocate的宾语是more time；to the initial review说明资源投向。 时间被作为有限资源安排给一项活动。more表示相对当前安排增加，但没有给出新增时长或资金批准。",
        "sourceRefs": [
          {
            "sourceId": "oewn-2025",
            "sourceVersion": "2025",
            "locator": "entries-a.json/allocate/v / allocate%2:40:00::",
            "supportedClaim": "distribute according to a plan or set apart for a special purpose",
            "url": "https://en-word.net/"
          }
        ],
        "title": "句子结构与当前所指"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "contrast",
        "dimensions": [
          "contrast"
        ],
        "text": "allocate是分配资源；estimate是估计需要多少。估计评审需要三小时，不等于日程已经给足三小时。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "容易混淆的地方"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "game-neighbors",
        "dimensions": [
          "languageGame",
          "englishNeighbors"
        ],
        "text": "应结合评审范围、参与者和已有日程讨论调整，并核对增加时间对其他事项的影响。 allocate time/resources to连接资源与用途；time allocation是分配结果；available capacity帮助检查分配能否兑现。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "讨论通常怎样继续"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "action",
        "dimensions": [
          "pragmaticAction"
        ],
        "text": "说话者在倡议调整时间安排，而不是报告调整已生效。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "说话者正在做什么"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "workplace",
